radv/directmesh: the PS5 and PS5 Slim

Their GPU (Oberon) is in the BC-250's chip family, CHIP_GFX1013, which DirectMesh supports; only its PCI ids are
missing from the list DirectMesh turns itself on for. Consoles report 1002:13fb or 1002:13db (a PS5 Slim with
13db confirmed DirectMesh working when forced, issue #62).
---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_directmesh.h b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_directmesh.h
index faf3e74..65780fb 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_directmesh.h
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_directmesh.h
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@ radv_directmesh_pci(uint16_t vendor, uint16_t device)
    if (vendor != 0x1002)
       return false;
    switch (device) {
+   case 0x13db: /* PS5 and PS5 Slim (Oberon), both GPU ids */
+   case 0x13fb:
    case 0x13fe:
    case 0x143f:
    case 0x7310: case 0x7312: case 0x7318: case 0x7319:
